hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15845","Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Zayd informed us, from al-Hasan, that al-Dahhak ibn Qays wrote to Qays ibn al-Haytham when Yazid ibn Muawiyah died: Peace be upon you; as for what follows, I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Before the Hour there will be trials like pieces of the dark night, trials like pieces of smoke; the heart of a man dies in them as his body dies; a man wakes a believer and sleeps a disbeliever, and sleeps a believer and wakes a disbeliever; peoples sell their share and their religion for a portion of this world. Yazid ibn Muawiyah has died, and you are our brothers and our kin, so do not act before us until we choose for ourselves."
